{
  "step1_summary": "- Chief complaint: New-onset headache starting yesterday (mid-morning).\n- Symptoms: Left-sided posterior (occipital) head pain; throbbing; built up gradually over a short period; severity 8/10. Not relieved by a dose of ibuprofen taken yesterday. No nausea, vomiting, photophobia, phonophobia, visual disturbance, tingling, numbness, weakness, fever, rash, or neck stiffness. No change with position, coughing, sneezing, bending. Slept last night. Hard to do normal work because of pain.\n- Past medical history: None reported.\n- Medications / allergies: Took ibuprofen (Nurofen) yesterday; otherwise none. No reported drug allergies.\n- Family / social history: Mother has hypertension and history of migraines. Lives with partner. Occupation: designer. Denies tobacco, alcohol, recreational drugs.\n- Vital signs / exam: No vitals recorded; no physical exam findings recorded.\n- Labs / imaging: None reported.",
